# Data Model: Enterprise Facility Manager

**Feature**: Complete migration and modernization of Facility 3D Manager UI
**Created**: 2026-01-08
**Status**: Phase 1 Design

This document defines the entity schemas and relationships for the enterprise facility manager system, derived from functional requirements in [spec.md](./spec.md).

---

## Entity Overview

The system manages 8 core entities:

1. **Facility** - Physical facility locations with 3D visualization data
2. **Zone** - Subdivisions within facilities (equipment areas, zones)
3. **Sensor** - IoT sensors monitoring facility metrics
4. **Alert** - System-generated notifications for anomalies
5. **Report** - ISO-compliant compliance reports
6. **User** - System users with role-based access
7. **MetricHistory** - Time-series sensor data for historical analysis
8. **ChatSession** - AI-powered chat interactions for insights

---

## 1. Facility Entity

**Description**: Represents a physical facility location with 3D model, geospatial coordinates, and operational status.

### Schema

```typescript
interface Facility {
  // Identity
  id: string; // UUID
  name: string;
  code: string; // Unique facility code (e.g., "CMI-01", "KKN-02")

  // Location
  location: {
    address: string;
    city: string;
    province: string;
    postalCode: string;
    coordinates: {
      latitude: number;
      longitude: number;
    };
  };

  // Operational
  status: 'operational' | 'warning' | 'critical' | 'offline';
  capacity: number; // Max capacity (units depend on facility type)
  utilization: number; // Current utilization percentage (0-100)

  // 3D Visualization
  model3D: {
    path: string; // Path to 3D model file or geometry data
    position: [number, number, number]; // [x, y, z]
    rotation: [number, number, number]; // [rx, ry, rz] in radians
    scale: [number, number, number]; // [sx, sy, sz]
  };

  // Metadata
  type: string; // e.g., "Battery Storage", "Shopping Mall", "Data Center"
  zoneCount: number;
  sensorCount: number;
  activeAlerts: number;

  // Timestamps
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  lastHealthCheck: Date;
}
```

### Relationships

- **One-to-Many**: Facility → Zones (1 facility contains N zones)
- **One-to-Many**: Facility → Sensors (1 facility contains N sensors)
- **One-to-Many**: Facility → Alerts (1 facility generates N alerts)
- **One-to-Many**: Facility → Reports (1 facility has N reports)
- **One-to-Many**: Facility → MetricHistory (1 facility has N metric records)

### Validation Rules

- `id`: Required, UUID format
- `name`: Required, 1-100 characters
- `code`: Required, unique, alphanumeric with hyphens
- `status`: Required, enum validation
- `capacity`: Required, positive number
- `utilization`: Required, 0-100 range
- `coordinates.latitude`: -90 to 90
- `coordinates.longitude`: -180 to 180
- `zoneCount`: Non-negative integer
- `sensorCount`: Non-negative integer

### Indexes (IndexedDB)

```typescript
// Dexie.js schema
facilities: {
  keyPath: 'id',
  indexes: [
    { name: 'code', keyPath: 'code', unique: true },
    { name: 'status', keyPath: 'status' },
    { name: 'type', keyPath: 'type' },
    { name: 'province', keyPath: 'location.province' }
  ]
}
```

---

## 2. Zone Entity

**Description**: Subdivisions within a facility representing equipment areas, storage sections, or monitoring zones. Used for 3D visualization and alert localization.

### Schema

```typescript
interface Zone {
  // Identity
  id: string; // UUID
  facilityId: string; // Foreign key to Facility
  name: string;
  code: string; // Unique within facility (e.g., "ZONE-A1", "BAY-03")

  // 3D Visualization
  geometry: {
    type: 'box' | 'cylinder' | 'sphere' | 'custom';
    position: [number, number, number]; // [x, y, z] in facility coordinate system
    dimensions: {
      width: number;
      height: number;
      depth: number;
    };
  };

  // Visual State
  color: string; // Hex color code (e.g., "#00FF00")
  opacity: number; // 0.0 - 1.0
  highlighted: boolean;

  // Operational
  status: 'normal' | 'warning' | 'critical' | 'maintenance';
  temperature?: number; // Optional current temperature
  humidity?: number; // Optional current humidity
  sensorCount: number;

  // Metadata
  category: string; // e.g., "Equipment", "Storage", "Access", "Safety"
  description?: string;

  // Timestamps
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  lastSensorUpdate?: Date;
}
```

### Relationships

- **Many-to-One**: Zone → Facility (N zones belong to 1 facility)
- **One-to-Many**: Zone → Sensors (1 zone contains N sensors)
- **One-to-Many**: Zone → Alerts (1 zone generates N alerts)

### Validation Rules

- `id`: Required, UUID format
- `facilityId`: Required, UUID format, must exist in Facility table
- `name`: Required, 1-50 characters
- `code`: Required, unique within facility
- `geometry.type`: Required, enum validation
- `geometry.position`: Required, 3-element array of numbers
- `geometry.dimensions`: Required, all positive numbers
- `color`: Required, valid hex color code (#RRGGBB)
- `opacity`: Required, 0.0-1.0 range
- `status`: Required, enum validation
- `temperature`: Optional, -50 to 100 (Celsius)
- `humidity`: Optional, 0-100 (percentage)

### Indexes (IndexedDB)

```typescript
zones: {
  keyPath: 'id',
  indexes: [
    { name: 'facilityId', keyPath: 'facilityId' },
    { name: '[facilityId+code]', keyPath: ['facilityId', 'code'], unique: true },
    { name: 'status', keyPath: 'status' },
    { name: 'category', keyPath: 'category' }
  ]
}
```

---

## 3. Sensor Entity

**Description**: IoT sensors monitoring environmental or operational metrics within zones.

### Schema

```typescript
interface Sensor {
  // Identity
  id: string; // UUID
  facilityId: string; // Foreign key to Facility
  zoneId: string; // Foreign key to Zone
  name: string;
  deviceId: string; // Physical device identifier

  // Configuration
  type: 'temperature' | 'humidity' | 'pressure' | 'vibration' | 'power' | 'air_quality' | 'custom';
  unit: string; // e.g., "°C", "%", "Pa", "Hz", "kW", "ppm"
  updateInterval: number; // Seconds between readings

  // Current State
  currentValue: number;
  lastReading: Date;
  status: 'active' | 'inactive' | 'error' | 'maintenance';

  // Thresholds
  thresholds: {
    critical: { min?: number; max?: number };
    warning: { min?: number; max?: number };
    normal: { min: number; max: number };
  };

  // Metadata
  manufacturer?: string;
  model?: string;
  firmwareVersion?: string;
  installDate?: Date;
  lastCalibration?: Date;

  // Timestamps
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
}
```

### Relationships

- **Many-to-One**: Sensor → Facility (N sensors belong to 1 facility)
- **Many-to-One**: Sensor → Zone (N sensors belong to 1 zone)
- **One-to-Many**: Sensor → MetricHistory (1 sensor generates N historical records)
- **One-to-Many**: Sensor → Alerts (1 sensor triggers N alerts)

### Validation Rules

- `id`: Required, UUID format
- `facilityId`: Required, UUID format, must exist in Facility table
- `zoneId`: Required, UUID format, must exist in Zone table
- `name`: Required, 1-100 characters
- `deviceId`: Required, unique across system
- `type`: Required, enum validation
- `unit`: Required, 1-20 characters
- `updateInterval`: Required, positive integer (seconds)
- `currentValue`: Required, number
- `status`: Required, enum validation
- `thresholds.normal`: Required, min < max

### Indexes (IndexedDB)

```typescript
sensors: {
  keyPath: 'id',
  indexes: [
    { name: 'facilityId', keyPath: 'facilityId' },
    { name: 'zoneId', keyPath: 'zoneId' },
    { name: 'deviceId', keyPath: 'deviceId', unique: true },
    { name: 'type', keyPath: 'type' },
    { name: 'status', keyPath: 'status' }
  ]
}
```

---

## 4. Alert Entity

**Description**: System-generated notifications for sensor threshold violations, system anomalies, or operational issues.

### Schema

```typescript
interface Alert {
  // Identity
  id: string; // UUID
  facilityId: string; // Foreign key to Facility
  zoneId?: string; // Optional foreign key to Zone
  sensorId?: string; // Optional foreign key to Sensor

  // Classification
  type: 'threshold_violation' | 'system_error' | 'maintenance_required' | 'anomaly_detected' | 'custom';
  severity: 'critical' | 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' | 'info';
  category: 'safety' | 'operational' | 'environmental' | 'equipment' | 'system';

  // Content
  title: string;
  description: string;
  metadata: Record<string, any>; // Additional context (sensor values, error codes, etc.)

  // State
  status: 'active' | 'acknowledged' | 'resolved' | 'dismissed';
  priority: number; // 1-10 (10 = highest)

  // Assignment
  assignedTo?: string; // User ID
  acknowledgedBy?: string; // User ID
  acknowledgedAt?: Date;
  resolvedBy?: string; // User ID
  resolvedAt?: Date;

  // Actions
  recommendedActions: string[]; // Array of action descriptions
  resolutionNotes?: string;

  // Timestamps
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  expiresAt?: Date; // Auto-dismiss date
}
```

### Relationships

- **Many-to-One**: Alert → Facility (N alerts belong to 1 facility)
- **Many-to-One**: Alert → Zone (N alerts belong to 1 zone, optional)
- **Many-to-One**: Alert → Sensor (N alerts triggered by 1 sensor, optional)
- **Many-to-One**: Alert → User (assigned/acknowledged/resolved by user)

### Validation Rules

- `id`: Required, UUID format
- `facilityId`: Required, UUID format, must exist in Facility table
- `zoneId`: Optional, UUID format, must exist in Zone table if provided
- `sensorId`: Optional, UUID format, must exist in Sensor table if provided
- `type`: Required, enum validation
- `severity`: Required, enum validation
- `category`: Required, enum validation
- `title`: Required, 1-200 characters
- `description`: Required, 1-2000 characters
- `status`: Required, enum validation
- `priority`: Required, 1-10 range
- `recommendedActions`: Array of strings

### State Transitions

```
active → acknowledged → resolved
       ↘ dismissed
```

### Indexes (IndexedDB)

```typescript
alerts: {
  keyPath: 'id',
  indexes: [
    { name: 'facilityId', keyPath: 'facilityId' },
    { name: 'zoneId', keyPath: 'zoneId' },
    { name: 'sensorId', keyPath: 'sensorId' },
    { name: 'severity', keyPath: 'severity' },
    { name: 'status', keyPath: 'status' },
    { name: 'createdAt', keyPath: 'createdAt' },
    { name: '[facilityId+status]', keyPath: ['facilityId', 'status'] },
    { name: '[severity+createdAt]', keyPath: ['severity', 'createdAt'] }
  ]
}
```

---

## 5. Report Entity

**Description**: ISO-compliant compliance reports (27001, 14001, 9001, 45001) generated for facilities.

### Schema

```typescript
interface Report {
  // Identity
  id: string; // UUID
  facilityId: string; // Foreign key to Facility
  reportNumber: string; // Unique report number (e.g., "ISO-27001-2026-001")

  // Classification
  standard: 'ISO-27001' | 'ISO-14001' | 'ISO-9001' | 'ISO-45001';
  type: 'audit' | 'compliance' | 'incident' | 'performance' | 'custom';
  classification: 'public' | 'internal' | 'confidential' | 'restricted';

  // Content
  title: string;
  summary: string;
  findings: ReportFinding[];
  recommendations: string[];
  attachments: ReportAttachment[];

  // Metadata
  status: 'draft' | 'pending_review' | 'approved' | 'published' | 'archived';
  period: {
    startDate: Date;
    endDate: Date;
  };

  // Audit Trail
  createdBy: string; // User ID
  reviewedBy?: string; // User ID
  approvedBy?: string; // User ID
  publishedBy?: string; // User ID

  // Timestamps
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  reviewedAt?: Date;
  approvedAt?: Date;
  publishedAt?: Date;
}

interface ReportFinding {
  id: string;
  category: string;
  severity: 'critical' | 'major' | 'minor' | 'observation';
  description: string;
  evidence: string[];
  recommendation: string;
}

interface ReportAttachment {
  id: string;
  filename: string;
  mimeType: string;
  size: number; // bytes
  url: string;
  uploadedAt: Date;
}
```

### Relationships

- **Many-to-One**: Report → Facility (N reports belong to 1 facility)
- **Many-to-One**: Report → User (created/reviewed/approved by users)

### Validation Rules

- `id`: Required, UUID format
- `facilityId`: Required, UUID format, must exist in Facility table
- `reportNumber`: Required, unique, format pattern validation
- `standard`: Required, enum validation
- `type`: Required, enum validation
- `classification`: Required, enum validation
- `title`: Required, 1-200 characters
- `summary`: Required, 1-5000 characters
- `status`: Required, enum validation
- `period.startDate`: Required, must be before endDate
- `period.endDate`: Required, must be after startDate
- `createdBy`: Required, UUID format, must exist in User table

### State Transitions

```
draft → pending_review → approved → published
                      ↘ draft (rejected)
                                 ↘ archived
```

### Indexes (IndexedDB)

```typescript
reports: {
  keyPath: 'id',
  indexes: [
    { name: 'facilityId', keyPath: 'facilityId' },
    { name: 'reportNumber', keyPath: 'reportNumber', unique: true },
    { name: 'standard', keyPath: 'standard' },
    { name: 'status', keyPath: 'status' },
    { name: 'classification', keyPath: 'classification' },
    { name: 'createdAt', keyPath: 'createdAt' },
    { name: '[facilityId+standard]', keyPath: ['facilityId', 'standard'] }
  ]
}
```

---

## 6. User Entity

**Description**: System users with role-based access control and authentication.

### Schema

```typescript
interface User {
  // Identity
  id: string; // UUID
  username: string; // Unique username
  email: string; // Unique email

  // Profile
  firstName: string;
  lastName: string;
  displayName: string; // Computed: firstName + lastName
  avatar?: string; // URL to avatar image
  phone?: string;

  // Authentication
  passwordHash: string; // Hashed password (never stored plaintext)
  emailVerified: boolean;
  twoFactorEnabled: boolean;

  // Authorization
  role: 'admin' | 'facility_manager' | 'operator' | 'auditor' | 'viewer';
  permissions: string[]; // Array of permission strings (e.g., "facilities:read", "alerts:write")
  facilityAccess: string[]; // Array of Facility IDs user can access

  // Session
  lastLogin?: Date;
  loginCount: number;
  sessionToken?: string; // Current session token

  // Preferences
  preferences: {
    language: string; // e.g., "en-US", "th-TH"
    timezone: string; // e.g., "Asia/Bangkok"
    theme: 'light' | 'dark' | 'auto';
    notifications: {
      email: boolean;
      inApp: boolean;
      alertSeverities: ('critical' | 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' | 'info')[];
    };
  };

  // Status
  status: 'active' | 'inactive' | 'suspended' | 'deleted';

  // Timestamps
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  deletedAt?: Date; // Soft delete
}
```

### Relationships

- **One-to-Many**: User → Alerts (1 user handles N alerts)
- **One-to-Many**: User → Reports (1 user creates N reports)
- **One-to-Many**: User → ChatSessions (1 user has N chat sessions)
- **Many-to-Many**: User ↔ Facilities (N users access N facilities via `facilityAccess` array)

### Validation Rules

- `id`: Required, UUID format
- `username`: Required, unique, 3-50 characters, alphanumeric + underscore
- `email`: Required, unique, valid email format
- `firstName`: Required, 1-50 characters
- `lastName`: Required, 1-50 characters
- `role`: Required, enum validation
- `permissions`: Array of permission strings
- `facilityAccess`: Array of valid Facility UUIDs
- `preferences.language`: Required, ISO 639-1 format
- `preferences.timezone`: Required, IANA timezone format
- `status`: Required, enum validation

### Indexes (IndexedDB)

```typescript
users: {
  keyPath: 'id',
  indexes: [
    { name: 'username', keyPath: 'username', unique: true },
    { name: 'email', keyPath: 'email', unique: true },
    { name: 'role', keyPath: 'role' },
    { name: 'status', keyPath: 'status' }
  ]
}
```

---

## 7. MetricHistory Entity

**Description**: Time-series historical sensor data for trend analysis, reporting, and anomaly detection.

### Schema

```typescript
interface MetricHistory {
  // Identity (composite key)
  facilityId: string; // Foreign key to Facility
  sensorId: string; // Foreign key to Sensor
  timestamp: Date; // Measurement timestamp

  // Measurement
  metricType: string; // Sensor type (temperature, humidity, etc.)
  value: number;
  unit: string;

  // Quality
  quality: 'good' | 'uncertain' | 'bad'; // Data quality indicator
  interpolated: boolean; // True if value was interpolated

  // Metadata
  source: 'sensor' | 'manual' | 'calculated' | 'imported';
  batchId?: string; // For bulk imports
}
```

### Relationships

- **Many-to-One**: MetricHistory → Facility (N records belong to 1 facility)
- **Many-to-One**: MetricHistory → Sensor (N records belong to 1 sensor)

### Validation Rules

- `facilityId`: Required, UUID format, must exist in Facility table
- `sensorId`: Required, UUID format, must exist in Sensor table
- `timestamp`: Required, Date object
- `metricType`: Required, string matching sensor types
- `value`: Required, number
- `unit`: Required, string
- `quality`: Required, enum validation
- `source`: Required, enum validation

### Indexes (IndexedDB)

**Critical for query performance on time-series data**:

```typescript
metricHistory: {
  keyPath: ['facilityId', 'sensorId', 'timestamp'], // Composite key
  indexes: [
    { name: 'facilityId', keyPath: 'facilityId' },
    { name: 'sensorId', keyPath: 'sensorId' },
    { name: 'timestamp', keyPath: 'timestamp' },
    { name: '[facilityId+timestamp]', keyPath: ['facilityId', 'timestamp'] },
    { name: '[sensorId+timestamp]', keyPath: ['sensorId', 'timestamp'] },
    { name: 'metricType', keyPath: 'metricType' }
  ]
}
```

### Data Retention Policy

- **Granular data**: Last 30 days (1-minute resolution)
- **Aggregated data**: 31-365 days (15-minute averages)
- **Long-term data**: 1+ years (daily averages)

**Aggregation Strategy** (automatic cleanup):
```typescript
// Daily aggregation job
async function aggregateOldData() {
  const thirtyDaysAgo = Date.now() - (30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);

  // Get old granular data
  const oldData = await db.metricHistory
    .where('timestamp')
    .below(thirtyDaysAgo)
    .toArray();

  // Aggregate to 15-minute intervals
  const aggregated = aggregateByInterval(oldData, 15 * 60 * 1000);

  // Replace granular with aggregated
  await db.metricHistory.bulkDelete(oldData.map(d => [d.facilityId, d.sensorId, d.timestamp]));
  await db.metricHistoryAggregated.bulkPut(aggregated);
}
```

---

## 8. ChatSession Entity

**Description**: AI-powered chat interactions for facility insights, recommendations, and troubleshooting assistance.

### Schema

```typescript
interface ChatSession {
  // Identity
  id: string; // UUID
  userId: string; // Foreign key to User
  facilityId?: string; // Optional context - if chat is facility-specific

  // Content
  title: string; // Auto-generated or user-provided
  messages: ChatMessage[];

  // State
  status: 'active' | 'archived';
  context: {
    entities: {
      facilities: string[]; // Facility IDs discussed
      zones: string[]; // Zone IDs discussed
      alerts: string[]; // Alert IDs discussed
    };
    topics: string[]; // Keywords/tags for search
  };

  // Timestamps
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  lastMessageAt: Date;
}

interface ChatMessage {
  id: string; // UUID
  role: 'user' | 'assistant' | 'system';
  content: string;
  timestamp: Date;

  // AI Context
  model?: string; // e.g., "gemini-pro"
  tokens?: number; // Token count
  references?: {
    facilityId?: string;
    zoneId?: string;
    alertId?: string;
    sensorId?: string;
  };

  // Feedback
  helpful?: boolean; // User feedback
  feedbackComment?: string;
}
```

### Relationships

- **Many-to-One**: ChatSession → User (N sessions belong to 1 user)
- **Many-to-One**: ChatSession → Facility (N sessions reference 1 facility, optional)

### Validation Rules

- `id`: Required, UUID format
- `userId`: Required, UUID format, must exist in User table
- `facilityId`: Optional, UUID format, must exist in Facility table if provided
- `title`: Required, 1-200 characters
- `status`: Required, enum validation
- `messages`: Array of ChatMessage objects
- `messages[].role`: Required, enum validation
- `messages[].content`: Required, 1-10000 characters
- `messages[].timestamp`: Required, Date object

### Indexes (IndexedDB)

```typescript
chatSessions: {
  keyPath: 'id',
  indexes: [
    { name: 'userId', keyPath: 'userId' },
    { name: 'facilityId', keyPath: 'facilityId' },
    { name: 'status', keyPath: 'status' },
    { name: 'createdAt', keyPath: 'createdAt' },
    { name: 'lastMessageAt', keyPath: 'lastMessageAt' },
    { name: '[userId+status]', keyPath: ['userId', 'status'] }
  ]
}
```

